Avian is the chirping, whistling language of the aarakocra and other bird-folk
of The World. It incorporates trills, clicks, and melodic phrases that surface
dwellers often mistake for birdsong.

The language has an extensive vocabulary for aerial concepts - wind currents,
altitudes, diving techniques, and nest-building - but struggles to express
ideas related to underground or aquatic environments. Speakers often
accompany their words with subtle wing and feather movements that add
nuance.

Learning Avian opens communication with the proud aarakocra and their kin,
who rarely deign to learn surface tongues. Their mountain aeries hold ancient
knowledge that few groundwalkers ever access.

